1
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,720
(The Underworld)

2
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:12,020
(Shen Yanlin)

3
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:17,800
♪Cruel world, where trust runs thin♪
(Ling Che)

4
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:22,300
♪Blades clash. Who will rise above?♪
(Shuangdao Hui)

5
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:28,460
♪Behind every smile, danger waits♪
(Dongshan Tai)

6
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:30,500
(Fei Liu)

7
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:35,560
♪Know your limits, know your worth♪
(Luo Song)

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,740
♪Stand strong against the raging tide♪
(Annie)

9
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:44,260
♪Ask how many times I've lost my way♪

10
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:49,130
♪Storms rage on the road to power♪

11
00:00:49,130 --> 00:00:53,700
♪Let old promises fade into memory♪

12
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:58,380
♪Alone and fearless, I won't back down♪

13
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:02,040
♪Power is a crown forged in blood♪

14
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:09,000
♪Brotherhood is shelter from the storm♪

15
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:15,740
=The Underworld=

16
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:18,660
=Episode 5=

17
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:19,940
(1994)

18
00:01:19,959 --> 00:01:20,480
Boss Che.

19
00:01:21,519 --> 00:01:22,200
Thirsty?

20
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:29,879
Have a Coke?

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:36,680
Am I cool?

22
00:02:00,239 --> 00:02:01,040
Do you want to learn?

23
00:02:13,039 --> 00:02:13,639
Boss Che.

24
00:02:14,599 --> 00:02:15,120
So...

25
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,439
what are we waiting for here?

26
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,280
Waiting to collect parking fees.

27
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:20,639
Or what do you think? Girls?

28
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,759
Is collecting parking fees

29
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,919
all we do around here?

30
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,680
Boss Che, I was thinking,

31
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:32,960
our gang

32
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,680
may have bigger jobs to do.

33
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:37,439
Let me tell you something.

34
00:02:37,639 --> 00:02:38,639
If you wanna make it in this world,

35
00:02:39,759 --> 00:02:40,560
the first thing

36
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:42,639
you need to learn is
to keep your mouth shut.

37
00:02:49,919 --> 00:02:50,400
Boss Che.

38
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:52,599
You're amazing
with your fists and kicks.

39
00:02:53,159 --> 00:02:54,919
When are you gonna teach me?

40
00:02:54,919 --> 00:02:56,240
There's a car in the third row.

41
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:57,599
What color?

42
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:00,159
Third row...

43
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,439
There is no third row.

44
00:03:02,439 --> 00:03:03,240
You've been here long enough.

45
00:03:03,479 --> 00:03:05,039
What's the license plate number
of the car in the corner?

46
00:03:05,319 --> 00:03:05,840
I don't know.

47
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,439
You can't even do the basics.

48
00:03:07,439 --> 00:03:08,319
How are you supposed to survive?

49
00:03:08,759 --> 00:03:10,960
Memorize every license plate here first.

50
00:03:11,639 --> 00:03:12,400
Got it, Boss Che.

51
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,159
What's so hard about opening
a bottle cap?

52
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:24,320
(Stop)

53
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:49,680
Boss Che.

54
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:50,919
Something's up.

55
00:03:53,039 --> 00:03:54,400
I think someone's in there.

56
00:04:03,439 --> 00:04:04,240
I'll open it.

57
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,319
Don't get involved.

58
00:04:05,319 --> 00:04:07,280
I have to.
Someone could die in this heat.

59
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,639
Can you open locks too,
not just bottles?

60
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:14,400
Hurry.

61
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:16,560
Help!

62
00:04:22,959 --> 00:04:23,639
What are you doing?

63
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,000
Put the kid down.

64
00:04:25,959 --> 00:04:26,399
Boss Che.

65
00:04:26,879 --> 00:04:27,319
You go first.

66
00:04:50,199 --> 00:04:50,639
Boss Hui.

67
00:04:51,519 --> 00:04:51,959
Boss Hui.

68
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:00,079
Does the North Parking Lot

69
00:05:00,439 --> 00:05:01,920
belong to your Dongcheng Gang?

70
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:03,360
What's the problem?

71
00:05:03,959 --> 00:05:05,399
You've crossed the line.

72
00:05:06,199 --> 00:05:07,199
Your guy

73
00:05:07,959 --> 00:05:09,279
let my hostage go.

74
00:05:09,279 --> 00:05:10,879
Shuangdao Hui,
aren't you all about rules?

75
00:05:13,279 --> 00:05:13,839
Che.

76
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,360
Is that true?

77
00:05:16,959 --> 00:05:18,319
Boss Hui. I'm sorry.

78
00:05:19,879 --> 00:05:20,800
It was me, Boss Hui.

79
00:05:21,879 --> 00:05:23,240
I saw them kidnap a child.

80
00:05:23,639 --> 00:05:24,480
I just didn't like you.

81
00:05:24,839 --> 00:05:25,160
So you did it.

82
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,560
What now?

83
00:05:28,079 --> 00:05:29,000
What do you want to do?

84
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:30,360
Right.

85
00:05:30,879 --> 00:05:31,759
It's up to you.

86
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:33,240
The money.

87
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,319
Pay me back what I lost.

88
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:37,439
And your guy,

89
00:05:38,519 --> 00:05:39,160
I'm taking him with me.

90
00:05:46,399 --> 00:05:46,879
Bro.

91
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:49,680
I've been

92
00:05:50,439 --> 00:05:51,240
in this game for decades.

93
00:05:51,879 --> 00:05:52,800
I live by three rules.

94
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:54,759
First,

95
00:05:55,879 --> 00:05:56,720
I respect the rules.

96
00:05:57,399 --> 00:05:58,000
Second,

97
00:05:59,079 --> 00:06:00,000
I stand by loyalty.

98
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:01,720
Third,

99
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,519
I've got plenty of brothers.

100
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,439
Come in.

101
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,079
Fourth...

102
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,879
I thought you said there were three!

103
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,079
I just added a new one.

104
00:06:15,279 --> 00:06:16,600
From now on, I don't play by the rules.

105
00:06:17,199 --> 00:06:18,199
If I, Shuangdao Hui,

106
00:06:18,199 --> 00:06:19,759
let you take my brother away today...

107
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:20,920
Shuangdao Hui...

108
00:06:21,319 --> 00:06:22,279
Shuangdao Hui...

109
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,360
Listen carefully.

110
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:27,480
From now on,

111
00:06:28,199 --> 00:06:29,800
don't ever mess with me.

112
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,319
You better stay away

113
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,160
from that parking lot.

114
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,120
It is my turf now.

115
00:06:35,879 --> 00:06:37,160
Leave immediately.

116
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:38,279
(Loyalty)
Get lost!

117
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:41,519
Get out!

118
00:06:50,319 --> 00:06:50,759
Boss Hui.

119
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:52,279
I did

120
00:06:53,199 --> 00:06:54,000
this thing.

121
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,720
You saved my life today.

122
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,279
Punish me however you want.

123
00:06:58,839 --> 00:06:59,199
I'll take it.

124
00:06:59,959 --> 00:07:01,199
(Loyalty)
I grew up without parents,

125
00:07:01,759 --> 00:07:03,120
so I don't want those kids
to end up like me.

126
00:07:04,079 --> 00:07:05,519
That's why I don't think

127
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:06,800
what I did was wrong.

128
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,120
Maybe becoming a father changed me.

129
00:07:13,759 --> 00:07:15,319
That's why I despise

130
00:07:15,839 --> 00:07:16,759
people who traffic children.

131
00:07:18,759 --> 00:07:19,160
Then...

132
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:20,959
why are you still punishing us?

133
00:07:21,319 --> 00:07:22,519
I'm punishing you this time

134
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,040
not because you took the girl.

135
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,759
I'm punishing you for being reckless.

136
00:07:28,879 --> 00:07:30,199
You charge in without thinking.

137
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,959
All guts, no brains.

138
00:07:33,639 --> 00:07:34,600
Not an ounce of strategy.

139
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,959
If you leave a trail behind,

140
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,480
you're not a hero.

141
00:07:40,399 --> 00:07:41,360
You're just cannon fodder.

142
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:45,519
Boss Hui.

143
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:46,800
Actually,

144
00:07:47,399 --> 00:07:48,800
I did this on my own.

145
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,160
Punish me.

146
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,120
Remember this.

147
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,480
If you want to save someone,

148
00:07:55,319 --> 00:07:56,560
you have to become stronger first.

149
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:58,879
You have to be tougher.

150
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,199
Only then can you rise higher.

151
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,199
Never forget that.

152
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:30,720
(Dongcheng Tiger)

153
00:08:56,559 --> 00:08:57,440
Lin.

154
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,159
You're hurt.

155
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,240
I'm fine.

156
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,639
You're not.

157
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,440
This little injury

158
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:08,279
is nothing compared to what
Zhen The Madwoman did to me as a kid.

159
00:09:08,879 --> 00:09:10,080
Lin.

160
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,120
What is it?

161
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,159
Be gentle.

162
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,919
I will.

163
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:21,159
Easy. Easy.

164
00:09:25,759 --> 00:09:28,200
Feel better?

165
00:09:30,159 --> 00:09:30,879
Much better.

166
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,120
It doesn't hurt.

167
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,080
Not hurt.

168
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:46,080
Fu.

169
00:09:46,759 --> 00:09:47,480
Stay here.

170
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:49,559
Lin.

171
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:51,559
Lin.

172
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:52,720
Lin.

173
00:09:53,039 --> 00:09:53,559
Lin.

174
00:09:53,679 --> 00:09:54,200
Lin.

175
00:10:04,519 --> 00:10:05,039
Lin.

176
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,279
Didn't I tell you to stay inside?

177
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,639
Lin, this

178
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,679
smells amazing.

179
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:27,799
Goose.

180
00:10:30,919 --> 00:10:31,440
Come on.

181
00:10:31,559 --> 00:10:31,960
Let's eat.

182
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,399
Smells so good.

183
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,120
So good.

184
00:10:44,799 --> 00:10:45,480
It's good.

185
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:46,759
Eat, Lin.

186
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:48,960
You eat too.

187
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:49,919
I've got some.

188
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:55,260
(1999)

189
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:01,960
Wait, wait, wait.

190
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:03,840
Hello?

191
00:11:04,759 --> 00:11:05,279
Are you sure?

192
00:11:05,279 --> 00:11:06,399
Again, Lin.

193
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:07,480
Okay.

194
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:10,679
Dazui called.

195
00:11:11,799 --> 00:11:13,759
They said the dancers
at Ligong Nightclub

196
00:11:14,279 --> 00:11:15,360
do wear this kind of underwear.

197
00:11:16,159 --> 00:11:16,879
How did they find that out?

198
00:11:19,759 --> 00:11:21,000
There are so many dancers
at the nightclub.

199
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:22,600
How did they check?

200
00:11:23,159 --> 00:11:24,039
Ask them one by one?

201
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:25,600
"Did you lose your underwear?"

202
00:11:28,519 --> 00:11:29,559
There's always a way

203
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,639
around a problem.

204
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,200
Should we ask them one by one?

205
00:11:39,759 --> 00:11:40,879
I will, only if you do that.

206
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:42,279
I mean it.

207
00:11:42,519 --> 00:11:42,840
Come on.

208
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:43,919
Bring it on.

209
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,000
Only if you do that.

210
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:45,440
Fu can do that.

211
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:47,759
Do what?

212
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:50,200
Who? Fu?

213
00:11:51,879 --> 00:11:54,320
Where are you guys going?

214
00:11:54,519 --> 00:11:55,600
To ask about underwear.

215
00:12:15,519 --> 00:12:16,919
How are we supposed to find the trace?

216
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,919
Look carefully.

217
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:42,639
Stop staring, you creep.

218
00:12:42,919 --> 00:12:44,200
Look for it.

219
00:12:47,679 --> 00:12:48,480
That pretty girl...

220
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:50,799
the emerald she's wearing

221
00:12:52,399 --> 00:12:53,360
is ours, right?

222
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,200
It's our thing.

223
00:13:15,159 --> 00:13:16,840
Take a look, boss.
See which one you like.

224
00:13:20,279 --> 00:13:21,240
Keep the one in gold.

225
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:25,720
(Dancer, Annie)

226
00:13:47,799 --> 00:13:48,600
Beautiful.

227
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,240
Thank you.

228
00:13:54,879 --> 00:13:56,080
I meant your earrings.

229
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,320
You're funny.

230
00:14:03,159 --> 00:14:05,000
My brother really likes your earrings.

231
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:06,960
Name your price.

232
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,159
I don't think you really care about

233
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,519
these earrings.

234
00:14:13,879 --> 00:14:14,879
These earrings

235
00:14:15,039 --> 00:14:16,679
came from a street stall.

236
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:17,799
Ask me again,

237
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,600
and that's still my only answer.

238
00:14:23,159 --> 00:14:23,799
Can you add another answer?

239
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,279
Seems like you're not satisfied
with my service.

240
00:14:28,799 --> 00:14:29,799
I'll get you someone else.

241
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,519
Something's off about her.

242
00:14:59,279 --> 00:15:00,480
She's the one we're following, right?

243
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:01,440
Bro.

244
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,360
We've been following her
this whole time.

245
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,279
And you ask now?

246
00:15:04,279 --> 00:15:04,639
Let's go.

247
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:20,360
Mom.

248
00:15:20,759 --> 00:15:21,320
One bowl of wontons.

249
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:21,879
Let me do it.

250
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:22,559
It's hot. Be careful.

251
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:27,080
I want all the toppings. Hurry up.

252
00:15:35,159 --> 00:15:35,759
Thanks.

253
00:15:37,879 --> 00:15:38,679
Thanks.

254
00:15:41,519 --> 00:15:42,360
Let's talk.

255
00:15:51,919 --> 00:15:53,799
This old street used to be
under Hutou Jun's control.

256
00:15:55,519 --> 00:15:56,480
The earrings

257
00:15:57,759 --> 00:15:58,559
are from him, right?

258
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,000
Who gave them to me doesn't matter.

259
00:16:04,159 --> 00:16:05,080
What matters is

260
00:16:06,039 --> 00:16:07,200
I need to make a living.

261
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,559
And my family needs to survive.

262
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:14,159
Those injuries on your hands weren't
caused in just a day or two.

263
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:17,799
If you tell us the truth,

264
00:16:18,879 --> 00:16:19,679
we can help you.

265
00:16:20,759 --> 00:16:22,399
This street has changed hands
three times.

266
00:16:22,399 --> 00:16:23,799
And the stall fees went up
every single time.

267
00:16:24,519 --> 00:16:25,879
What makes you think you can help me?

268
00:16:26,159 --> 00:16:26,919
What makes us think that?

269
00:16:28,399 --> 00:16:29,759
Because we can make it disappear.

270
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:17,400
Whatever you want,

271
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:18,960
we can give you.

272
00:17:20,319 --> 00:17:20,960
Think about it.

273
00:17:23,119 --> 00:17:23,599
Here.

274
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,000
For the wontons.

275
00:17:26,559 --> 00:17:27,079
Let's go.

276
00:17:32,799 --> 00:17:33,519
Goodbye, ma'am.

277
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:34,599
Take care.

278
00:17:36,559 --> 00:17:37,200
Finished?

279
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:38,880
It was delicious. Thank you.

280
00:17:48,830 --> 00:17:53,560
♪Sometimes I don't even know
what I'm waiting for♪

281
00:17:55,780 --> 00:18:01,390
♪When the sun shines bright,
rain still falls from the sky♪

282
00:18:02,110 --> 00:18:05,070
♪Droplets on the leaves
reflect a rainbow♪

283
00:18:05,070 --> 00:18:08,070
♪I stood there and smiled♪

284
00:18:08,810 --> 00:18:13,800
♪Even I couldn't see what was hidden
in that smile♪

285
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:17,880
♪The city is vast,
with countless windows♪

286
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:19,550
♪Every one of them glowing with light♪

287
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:22,100
♪But none of them belong to me♪

288
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:25,020
♪I sit in the corner,
counting raindrops♪

289
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:26,650
♪One, two, three♪

290
00:18:26,650 --> 00:18:30,680
♪And the more I count,
the more I forget where I am♪

291
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:35,630
♪Someone asks me, "Are you okay?"♪

292
00:18:35,630 --> 00:18:38,360
♪I say, "I'm fine," in a quiet voice♪

293
00:18:39,430 --> 00:18:42,000
♪So quiet, like rain falling on leaves♪

294
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,290
♪And then nothing comes after♪

295
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:46,400
♪As if it never happened at all♪

296
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:48,470
♪There are tears hidden in my smile♪

297
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:51,840
♪But my tears make no sound♪

298
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:56,020
♪Calm like the surface of a lake♪

299
00:18:56,020 --> 00:18:59,190
♪Yet something beneath keeps moving♪

300
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:04,760
♪Maybe when the rain finally stops♪

301
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:07,760
♪I will finally see myself♪

302
00:19:08,430 --> 00:19:11,100
♪Maybe I could be a ray of light♪

303
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:14,220
♪Maybe I could be a rainbow♪
